From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] toplevel: Reserve nothing for an autohide panel on Wayland

While it was shown, an autohide panel kept its hidden strip as its exclusive
zone, 1 pixel, and reserved nothing once hidden, so a maximised window changed
size each time the panel came and went. On a floating panel it was worse: the
compositor counts a layer surface's margin in its zone, so the shown panel
reserved its 8 pixel gap too, and a maximised window stopped 9 pixels short of
the edge, with empty space under it.

An autohide panel comes and goes over the windows, so it reserves nothing, shown
or hidden. A panel without Autohide keeps its edge as it did, and X11's struts
don't change.
---
 mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c b/mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c
--- a/mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c
+++ b/mate-panel/panel-toplevel.c
@@ -1636,8 +1636,11 @@
 		 * reserved work area, so a reserved strip while hidden shows the
 		 * compositor's native background instead of the wallpaper. */
 		/* A panel that asks Caminito to hide it while a window overlaps
-		 * it can't keep its edge for itself, so it reserves nothing. */
+		 * it can't keep its edge for itself, so it reserves nothing. Nor
+		 * does an autohide panel, which comes and goes over the windows:
+		 * a floating one would reserve its gap as well as its strip. */
 		if (strut == 0 ||
+		    toplevel->priv->auto_hide ||
 		    toplevel->priv->state != PANEL_STATE_NORMAL ||
 		    wayland_panel_toplevel_has_intellihide (toplevel))
 			exclusive = 0;
